From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:33:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Connectivity: report empty stats, not an error, when there is
 no eBPF

Fourth and final layer of the same problem. With the BpfMap constructor and
BpfNetMaps.maybeThrow already fixed, the failure moved one level down:

  D TrafficControllerJni: native_swapActiveStatsMap failed, error code = 38
  W BpfNetMaps: Unable to swap active stats map ... kernel has no eBPF, continuing
  W BpfMap: pinned map netd_iface_index_name_map unavailable; leaving map invalid
  E BpfNetworkStats: get ifaceIndexName map fd failed: Function not implemented
  E NetworkStats: java.lang.IllegalStateException: java.io.IOException:
                  Failed to parse network stats

The consequence is much worse than lost statistics. NetworkStatsFactory turns
a non-zero return into IOException, NetworkStatsService wraps it in
IllegalStateException, and it unwinds out of
ConnectivityService.updateLinkProperties(). The rest of network setup is
abandoned, so the agent never leaves CONNECTING; createNativeNetwork() only
runs on CONNECTED, so netd never gets the network:

  E Netd: no such netId 100
  W ConnectivityService: Exception adding interface: Machine is not on the
                         network (code 64)
  D ConnectivityService: Setting DNS servers for network 100 to []

which is why WiFi associates, completes a full DHCP exchange with a valid
lease, and is then dropped ~18 seconds later having never been usable.

So on ENOSYS both parse entry points now return 0 with no stats rather than an
error. Per-UID accounting is unavailable on this kernel regardless; being
unable to connect at all is not an acceptable way to express that.
---
 .../libs/libnetworkstats/BpfNetworkStats.cpp  | 36 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/service-t/native/libs/libnetworkstats/BpfNetworkStats.cpp b/service-t/native/libs/libnetworkstats/BpfNetworkStats.cpp
index 9ebef4d6d..26ab8067b 100644
--- a/service-t/native/libs/libnetworkstats/BpfNetworkStats.cpp
+++ b/service-t/native/libs/libnetworkstats/BpfNetworkStats.cpp
@@ -189,6 +189,23 @@ int parseBpfNetworkStatsDetail(std::vector<stats_line>* lines,
     BpfMapRO<uint32_t, IfaceValue> ifaceIndexNameMap(IFACE_INDEX_NAME_MAP_PATH);
     if (!ifaceIndexNameMap.isValid()) {
         int ret = -errno;
+        if (errno == ENOSYS) {
+            // No bpf() syscall at all -- pre-4.x kernels predate it, so these pinned
+            // maps can never exist. Report success with no stats instead of an error.
+            //
+            // A non-zero return here becomes IOException("Failed to parse network
+            // stats") in NetworkStatsFactory, which unwinds through
+            // NetworkStatsService.notifyNetworkStatus() and out of
+            // ConnectivityService.updateLinkProperties(). That abandons the rest of
+            // network setup, so the agent never reaches CONNECTED, so
+            // createNativeNetwork() never runs, so netd has no network to attach
+            // routes to -- the device gets a DHCP lease and still cannot use it.
+            //
+            // Losing per-UID traffic accounting is the acceptable cost; being unable
+            // to connect at all is not.
+            ALOGW("%s: no eBPF on this kernel, reporting empty stats", __func__);
+            return 0;
+        }
         ALOGE("get ifaceIndexName map fd failed: %s", strerror(errno));
         return ret;
     }
@@ -265,7 +282,24 @@ int parseBpfNetworkStatsDev(std::vector<stats_line>* lines) {
     int ret = 0;
     BpfMapRO<uint32_t, IfaceValue> ifaceIndexNameMap(IFACE_INDEX_NAME_MAP_PATH);
     if (!ifaceIndexNameMap.isValid()) {
-        ret = -errno;
+        int ret = -errno;
+        if (errno == ENOSYS) {
+            // No bpf() syscall at all -- pre-4.x kernels predate it, so these pinned
+            // maps can never exist. Report success with no stats instead of an error.
+            //
+            // A non-zero return here becomes IOException("Failed to parse network
+            // stats") in NetworkStatsFactory, which unwinds through
+            // NetworkStatsService.notifyNetworkStatus() and out of
+            // ConnectivityService.updateLinkProperties(). That abandons the rest of
+            // network setup, so the agent never reaches CONNECTED, so
+            // createNativeNetwork() never runs, so netd has no network to attach
+            // routes to -- the device gets a DHCP lease and still cannot use it.
+            //
+            // Losing per-UID traffic accounting is the acceptable cost; being unable
+            // to connect at all is not.
+            ALOGW("%s: no eBPF on this kernel, reporting empty stats", __func__);
+            return 0;
+        }
         ALOGE("get ifaceIndexName map fd failed: %s", strerror(errno));
         return ret;
     }
